# The determinism check of the test mode (issue #21; tools/testmode_check.py): log in, walk a square,
# say something, log out, close. Written for the Tibia.cfg of tools/compare_traffic.py (an 800x600
# window) and the test account of notes/testserver.md (772001 / patella); the client logs in through
# tools/proxy.py, which records every packet.
#
# Times are virtual milliseconds; at pace 100 (real time) the server gets as much real time to answer
# as the script waits.
#
# The dumps (issue #22): dump writes the client's state (state-<NNN>.json, which testmode_check.py
# compares with client_state.py's reading of the same moment), frame the next frame of the Vulkan engine
# (frame-<NNN>.png); both need --test-out, which testmode_check.py passes.

pace 100

# The start screen: "Enter Game" (tools/login_client.py: the middle of the button is at
# (113, height - 220) of the client area).
wait 2000
dump
frame
click 113 B-220

# The login dialog: account, Tab, password, Return.
wait 1500
text "772001"
key Tab
text "patella"
dump
key Return

# The message of the day (the run's Tibia.cfg has LastMotD = 0), then the character list: Return takes
# the highlighted (first) character.
wait 3000
key Return
wait 2000
key Return

# In the game; Return again closes a "First Login" hint, or goes to the empty console line.
wait 4000
dump
frame
key Return

# A square: north, east, south, west, back where the character started.
wait 1000
key Up
wait 1500
key Right
wait 1500
key Down
wait 1500
key Left
wait 1500
dump

# Say something (Cipfried, the temple's NPC, answers "hello").
text "hello world"
key Return
wait 2000
dump
frame

# Log out (Ctrl+L), then close the client at the start screen.
key Ctrl+L
wait 4000
dump
quit
